# Production GHCR + rootless Docker

Canonical prose: [docs/deploy.md](../../docs/deploy.md) § GHCR pull auth. Contract:
[dockerComposeContract.test.ts](../../src/libs/deploy/dockerComposeContract.test.ts).

## Two constraints (both required)

1. **Isolated auth** — Actions must use per-run
   `DOCKER_CONFIG=/tmp/mitsailing-ghcr-<run_id>-<attempt>` for login, release, and
   logout. Do **not** write GHCR creds into shared host `~/.docker` (clobbers
   operators / concurrent deploys on logout).
2. **Rootless daemon** — An empty/isolated config has no rootless CLI context, so
   the CLI defaults to `/var/run/docker.sock`. When
   `/run/user/$(id -u)/docker.sock` exists, set
   `DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/$(id -u)/docker.sock` on the **same** remote
   shell as login and release.

The deploy user login shell is `/bin/sh` (dash). `chsh` needs a password from
this key, so login and release ssh remotes must run `bash -c '…'` (bash is
installed). Do not put `set -o pipefail` or `[[` in the dash payload.

## Anti-thrash (learned from #191 / #192)

| Tempting “fix” | Why it fails |
| --- | --- |
| Drop `DOCKER_CONFIG` → use host `~/.docker` | Restores rootless context but shared login/logout races (Sourcery). |
| Keep isolated config, omit `DOCKER_HOST` | GHCR login can succeed while Release fails on `/var/run/docker.sock`. |
| Only assert `DOCKER_CONFIG` **or** `/run/user/` loosely in tests | One side can regress without failing CI. |

Do **not** “simplify” to host-default config to fix rootless. Do **not** drop
`DOCKER_HOST` to keep isolation. Prefer short-lived `GITHUB_TOKEN` +
`packages: read` over a long-lived host PAT for routine deploys.

## Before claiming deploy PR done

1. Contract tests assert the **login and release** remote snippets both set
   `DOCKER_CONFIG` and the rootless `DOCKER_HOST` sock check together.
2. Unanswered actionable bot threads (Sourcery/CodeRabbit/etc.) are fixed or
   won’t-fixed with a reply — do not tell the user the PR is done while those
   remain open.
3. After merge, production Release must get past `pinning image …` without
   GHCR `denied` and without `unix:///var/run/docker.sock` on a rootless host.
